--- !u!114 &8581109798477538062
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'You can assign Light cookies in the Light component.


      1. In the <i>Project</i> Window, select <b>Light_Spot_1600lm.</b>


      2. In its <i>Inspector,</i> in the <b>Emission</b> foldout, select the Cookie property and remove the assigned texture.


      3. Undo this change.


      Notice how the light shape changed: the edges no longer had a smooth transition, and some fine details were lost around the center of the light.'
